  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REPONSE INTERSECTORIELLE POST CYCLONIQUE GAMANE DANS LA REGION DE SAVA, NORD DE MADAGASCAR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide multi-sectoral assistance to communities affected by Tropical Cyclone Gamane in the districts of Sambava, Antalaha, and Vohemar in Madagascar. The WASH component includes disinfecting and rehabilitating community water points, social and behavioral change activities, and distributing WASH kits and water treatment products. The Education component includes disinfecting classrooms, procuring, and delivering tents and tarpaulins for temporary classrooms, distributing school kits and blackboards, and social and behavioral change interventions to promote access and retention. The Child Protection component includes rapid protection assessments, social and behavioral change interventions to prevent gender-based violence and exploitation, as well as providing psycho-social support to children and their caregivers. The project provides life-saving assistance to 30,000 people, of whom 8,400 are women and 7,800 are girls. Additionally, 2,400 people with disabilities benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
